title: Analytics › Payer scorecard
route: /analytics
intro: One row per payer for the chosen period, and an 'All payers' row at the bottom to compare with. A payer row opens the Payer analysis panel; a count inside a row opens its cases.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Scroll to 'Payer scorecard'"
screen sc "Columns: 'Payer' (plan type), 'Decisions', 'Approval rate' with a small 12-month line, 'Denial rate', 'Approved in part', 'Average days', 'Past CMS time', 'Info requests', 'Appeals overturned', 'Trend'\nLakeshore 86%, Beacon 81%, Harborview 77%, Summit 74%, Evergreen 69%, Cardinal 63%, All payers 71%"
process p1 "'Trend' is the change in approval rate against the earlier period, an arrow and 'pts'\n'Past CMS time' is 'n/a' for payers the CMS time does not apply to\nA figure under 20 decisions shows a dash\nWith a payer picked, only that payer and 'All payers' show"

click c1 "Click a payer row, or Tab to the payer name and press Enter"
process p2 "Opens the Payer analysis panel for that payer\nFocus returns to the row when it closes"
goto g1 "Continues in: Analytics › Payer analysis panel"

group gCount "Counts inside a row"
  click c2 "Click 'Approved in part', 'Past CMS time', 'Info requests' or 'Appeals overturned'"
  process p3 "Opens the case list panel for that payer and figure\nThe row does not open as well"
endgroup
goto g2 "Continues in: Analytics › Case list panel"

process p4 "The 'All payers' row is the clinic's own average\nIt is not clickable\nThe footnote says payers are compared with the clinic, not with an outside benchmark"
end e1 "Scorecard read"

s1 --> sc --> p1
sc --> c1 --> p2 --> g1
sc --> c2 --> p3 --> g2
sc -.-> p4 --> e1
